---
/* The chi-square result on its own. No per-category numbers, because the
   ones I could show would be reconstructions rather than the real output. */
---
<figure class="reveal">
  <div class="panel">
    <p class="tick" style="margin:0 0 .9rem">Return rates across product categories</p>
    <p class="stat num">p &lt; 0.001</p>
    <p class="sub">Chi-square test of independence</p>
    <hr />
    <p class="expl">
      Uneven-looking bars are not a finding — sampling noise produces those
      routinely. The test is what separates a real difference from a plausible
      accident, and it is the difference between "this looks odd" and something
      a category manager can act on.
    </p>
  </div>
</figure>
<style>
  .stat{font-size:clamp(2rem,4.5vw,2.9rem);margin:0;line-height:1;color:var(--v5)}
  .sub{font-family:var(--f-mono);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.1em;text-transform:uppercase;
    color:var(--muted);margin:.5rem 0 0}
  hr{border:0;border-top:1px solid var(--line);margin:1.1rem 0}
  .expl{font-size:.9rem;color:var(--muted);margin:0}
</style>
